we tend to make them more childlike, more, you know, big eyes, for instance, or sometimes we use animals that are furry like the peril seal with older adults to comfort them. When you think about the military robotics, you want them to look strong and sturdy and capable. So how we trust an agent, really how it looks plays a big part of that. And certainly there's a lot of researchers looking at that. What other ways do human robot teams differ from all human teams? What are the particular challenges of working with robots? So I would say human, human teams, there is a lot of ways in which we communicate.

13
