14
00:08:27.000 --> 00:09:00.000
I think another issue is when we study these robots in the lab, usually it's one and done. A participant comes into the lab or even maybe a group of participants comes into the lab and then they leave. Or sometimes we have the ability to study robots for, you know, have participants come a few times or put a robot into a home or into a classroom, but we don't have these really long extended interactions. So we want to really look at that. I think the last thing I would say is field studies. So having the robots out working in the

